meta {
  name: 07 Query an intermediate gate
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/factgraph/{{ruleset_id}}/query
  body: json
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "targets": ["/grossIncomeLimit"],
    "entities": {
      "/members": [
        {
          "id": "applicant",
          "/members/*/age": 30,
          "/members/*/isImmigrationEligible": true,
          "/members/*/isElderly": false,
          "/members/*/isDisabled": false,
          "/members/*/isHigherEdStudent": false
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

docs {
  You don't have to target the top-level answer. Any fact in the graph
  is queryable.

  Here we ask for `/grossIncomeLimit` — the dollar threshold this
  household would have to stay under to pass the gross income test —
  with just enough member info to compute household size. Useful for
  diagnostic UIs ("what threshold am I being compared against?")
  without having to feed the full intake.

  Other intermediate gates worth trying as targets:
    - `/meetsAssetTest`
    - `/grossIncomeEligible`
    - `/netMonthlyIncome`
    - `/standardDeduction`
    - `/members/*/isEligibleMember` (returns per-member array)

  Per-member targets return values as an array of {memberId, value}
  objects so callers can correlate to specific rows in their input.
}
